      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely, focusing on a brief yet comprehensive memo sounds perfect. Here's a suggested outline for your memo on workplace ergonomics:\n\n1. Subject: Importance of Ergonomic Workstation Setups for Preventing RSI\n2. Greetings and Introduction\n3. Explanation of Recommended Ergonomic Ergonomics Practices:\n   - Proper chair and desk heights\n   - Optimal screen position and monitor distance\n   - Desk accessories placement\n   - Correct keyboard and mouse usage and placement\n   - Footrest use\n4. Encouragement to Review and Tailor Their Ergonomic Setup\n5. Offering Resources for Further Assistance (such as company-provided ergonomic assessments)\n6. Reminder of the company’s support in maintaining a healthy work environment\n7. Call-to-Action for Employees to Share Ergonomic Issues With HR Support\n8. Closing Remarks and Commitment to Employee Well-being\n\nDon't forget to personalize your tone to both professional and approachable, emphasizing the company's commitment to your team’s health and well-being.",
